IPv6 ISP–Customer Lab: ULA P2P Peering with Public IPv6 Loopbacks
📌 Project Overview

This lab demonstrates a basic ISP–Customer IPv6 architecture where:

ISP and Customer are connected using a ULA IPv6 point-to-point link.
Both ISP and Customer have a Public IPv6 address on Loopback0.
Static routes are configured on both routers.
Public IPv6 Loopback addresses are reachable through the private/ULA transit link.
The lab simulates a simplified real-world ISP Customer connectivity scenario.

Note: IPv6 does not use RFC1918-style private addresses like IPv4. This lab uses ULA (Unique Local Address) from FC00::/7, specifically the fd00::/8 range, for the ISP–Customer P2P link.

