🎯 Learning Objective

The main objective of this lab is to understand how an ISP and customer router can establish IPv6 connectivity using a ULA-based point-to-point transit network, while maintaining public IPv6 addressing on Loopback interfaces and exchanging reachability through static routes.

This provides the foundation for more advanced ISP IPv6 routing, BGP, prefix delegation, and dual-stack network designs.

📌 Important Note

The 2001:db8::/32 prefix is reserved for documentation and examples. It is intentionally used in this lab and should not be used as real Internet-routable addressing in a production network.
